# Agent handoff

**Authoritative workflow:** `.cursor/rules/development-workflow.mdc`. Mandatory multi-agent handoffs and duplicate review stages are **removed**. One coding agent completes implementation, then one Security/QA review pass (rule `08`). This rule covers optional stop/reporting only. It does not change product behavior in `01`–`07`.

## When to stop

Stop implementing only for:

- Genuine access blockers
- Material scope decisions needing user input
- Final human approval (merge/deploy)

Do not weaken `PERMISSION_ENFORCEMENT`, `MULTITENANT_ENFORCEMENT`, reorder `server.js` middleware, edit vault crypto, or change existing `ROUTE_GROUPS` to ship faster. Security review is required when those areas are touched (development-workflow.mdc, rule `08`).

## Optional completion block

When summarizing a completed stage, you may use these fields (values may be `none` / `yes` / `no` as appropriate):

```
STATUS: blocked | done | needs-review
TASK: <one-line summary>
FILES CHANGED: <paths or none>
TESTS: <commands run and result, or none>
REVIEW: <Security/QA pass outcome; note if not independent>
REASON: <why stopped, or what remains>
RISKS: <tenant, permission, secrets, honesty, boot, none>
MODEL: <catalog slug or inherit>
MODEL SOURCE: frontmatter | lead-override | inherit | cursor-fallback
ESCALATION REASON: <none | trigger from rule 11>
```

- Implementation complete, review pending: `STATUS: needs-review`.
- Review complete: open or update the PR (rule `10`). Agents do not merge. **You approve → main**.
- Record `MODEL` / `MODEL SOURCE` / `ESCALATION REASON` when applicable. Never put API keys in this block.

## STATUS meanings

| STATUS | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `done` | Implementation and review complete; PR ready for user |
| `needs-review` | Implementation claimed done; Security/QA review not yet complete |
| `blocked` | Cannot proceed (missing env, user decision, failed tests) |
